  "prefLabel": "Env-Wr 101.41 Regulatory discharge capacity",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wr 101.41 “Regulatory discharge capacity” means the discharge capacity of a dam when the water is one foot below maximum pool level without the benefit of manual operations.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wr 100) #13979, eff 5-24-24",
